  "proof": {
    "bound": "Disjoint source JSON grammar tokens cover the payload. Strings and keys decode to no more bytes than their original content; each decoded byte requires at most six output bytes, with original quotes. Booleans/null are unchanged. Structural tokens cannot increase and duplicate object keys only discard entries. Integers fit 20 bytes and finite floats fit the 24-byte formatter. Thus each contribution is at most 32 times original bytes. The complete source line dominates the inline payload. Exact fallback remains for longer lines.",
